cess Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Excel SDK\nDescription: Various Microsoft Excel activities are added to enhance the Microsoft Excel SDK.  You can now use the Get Sensitivity Label ID activity to retrieve the sensitivity label ID of the current workbook, the Set Sensitivity activity to set a sensitivity to the current workbook, the Get UsedRange Row (from file) to retrieve the row index of the used range in the active worksheet, the Get UsedRange Column (from file) to retrieve the column index of the used range in the active worksheet and the Get Table Range Definition to retrieve the range definition of a named table in the active worksheet.  See Excel SDK and Best Practices for Excel Activities - Get Sensitivity Label ID.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-03\nValid as Of: 2025-03-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1305 ---\nComponent: SAP Intelligent Robotic Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Microsoft 365 Cloud SDK\nDescription: Various Microsoft Excel Online activities are added to enhance the Microsoft 365 SDK.  You can now use the Get UsedRange Row activity to retrieve the row index of the used range in an active excel worksheet and the Get UsedRange Column activity to retrieve the column index or name of the used range in the active excel worksheet.  See Microsoft 365 Cloud SDK.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-03\nValid as Of: 2025-03-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1306 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: SAP BTP Operator module: Update to version 1.2.0\nDescription: With this version, we have enabled customization of the sap-btp-manager Secret. Now, you can manage your own SAP BTP Operator's default configuration.  For more information, see Customizing the Default Credentials and Access.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1307 ---\nComponent: Region\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: US West (Oregon)\nDescription: US West (Oregon) (cf-us11) is available as a new region running on Amazon Web Services for use with enterprise accounts. See Regions and API Endpoints Available for the Cloud Foundry Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-28\nValid as Of: 2025-02-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1308 ---\nComponent: SAP Translation Hub\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle:   Support for video subtitle formats .srt and .vtt  \nDescription:   Document Translation now supports two of the most common text formats used for subtitles or closed captions: SRT (or .srt), also known as SubRip files, and VTT (or .vtt), known as Web Video Text Track (WebVTT) files. Users can get translations via the Document Translation user interface or use the APIs.   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-28\nValid as Of: 2025-02-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1309 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support of Verifiable Presentations to Include Verifiable Credentials with Embedded Proofs\nDescription: Now, you can create a verifiable presentation with verifiable credentials that have an embedded proof.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025\",592\n99,\"--- Record 501 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: CAPTCHA Protection\nDescription: Tenant administrator can enable CAPTCHA protection for the phone verification pages of the application. See Enable Google reCAPTCHA for Application Forms and Enable MTCaptcha for Application Forms.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-09\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: 28039\n\n--- Record 502 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Off-Cycle Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-09\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: 28039\n\n--- Record 503 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.43.1\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      Logs: Besides FluentBit, you can now also use OTLP as output for you LogPipeline resources. Based on an OTel Collector, you can tail logs from stdout/stderr, as well as push logs from applications. The gateway enriches your log data in the same way as for traces and metrics. For details, see Application Logs (#556).      Logs, Metrics, and Traces: For all your pipelines using an OTLP output, you can centrally configure enriching the data with Pod labels, so that the data gets k8s.pod.label.label attributes. For details, see Data Enrichment (#2195).      Traces and Metrics: Update to OTel Collector 0.128.0 (#2221).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 504 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pricing – Corrected Condition Base Calculation for Conditions with Multiple Counters\nDescription: When a condition had multiple counters and the step number was set to zero for that condition, the condition base incorrectly included results from subsequent steps. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 505 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pricing – Validation Fix for Zero-Value Conditions in Price Agreement\nDescription: When a condition was passed with a value of 0.000 and the plus/minus flag was set to negative in the condition type customizing, it incorrectly triggered a validation error in the Price agreement scenario. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 506 ---\nComponent: Personalized Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Overall Improvements\nDescription: There have been several code, stability, and performance improvements.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 507 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2025.14\nDescription: New and changed features are available for administration, data cataloging, data integration, data marketplace, data modeling, data privacy and protection, and space management.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2025.14. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 508 ---\nComponent: Responsibility Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Data Centers\nDescription: The Responsibility Management Service is now also available in the following regions:  AWS: EU12 - Europe (Frankfurt)  Google Cloud Platform: US30 - US Central (IA)  Google Cloud Platform: EU30 - Europe (Frankfurt)  See Pricing and Regions Information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-14\nValid as Of: 2025-07-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 509 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Advanced Functions for Decisions\nDescription: You can now use a new function, TRUNC in your decisions. See Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-07\nValid as Of: 2025-07-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 510 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Availibility of the Externalization feature on Edge Integration Cell\nDescription: You can now use the externalization feature to define API policies that can retrieve externalized configuration values during runtime. These parameters can be utilized later without modifying the standard API artifact. For more information, see Externalize Parameter for API Artifact.\n\",234\n260,\"--- Record 1771 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Command Line Interface\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Installation Script now Available for Downloading and Installing the Latest Version of the btp CLI Client\nDescription: Easy to use installation scripts are now available for all supported platforms:  Microsoft Windows (amd64)  Apple macOS (amd64 and arm64)  Linux (amd64 and arm64)    The installation scripts automate and guide you through the installation experience. See Download and Start Using the btp CLI Client.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-26\nValid as Of: 2024-12-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1772 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 44.9.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 44.5.0 to 44.9.0.      https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v44.9.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v44.8.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deploy